  "result": {
    "summary": "Implemented a default-off v6legacyv4obs training contract: repaired integer-chip v6 rules, legacy v4 observation and slot semantics, v6-table-exact action restriction, explicit checkpoint/resume metadata, and bridge deployment loading. Deterministic 50,000-state four-street audit preserved Standard10 greedy physical action 100% with zero removed greedy actions; 182 tests passed. Zero training and Slumbot hands.",
    "conclusion": "The historical Standard10 transfer loss is a combined observation/action-slot contract issue, with preflop slot semantics especially material. A trainable compatibility mode can now initialize from Standard10 without naive v6 rebinding disruption while still enforcing repaired physical rules and deployable actions.",
